prompt.text:
Create a pure TypeScript module for sorting and paging sensor readings.

Export these declarations:

```ts
export interface Reading {
  readonly id: string;
  readonly value: number;
  readonly recordedAt: number;
  readonly station: string;
}
export type ReadingSort = "id" | "value" | "recordedAt";
export interface ReadingQuery {
  readonly page: number;
  readonly pageSize: number;
  readonly sortBy: ReadingSort;
  readonly direction: "asc" | "desc";
}
export interface ReadingPage {
  readonly items: Reading[];
  readonly page: number;
  readonly pageSize: number;
  readonly totalItems: number;
  readonly totalPages: number;
}
export function queryReadings(source: readonly Reading[], query: ReadingQuery): ReadingPage;
```

`page` is one-based and must be an integer at least 1. `pageSize` must be an integer from 1 through 100. Every reading must have a nonempty ID and station, finite value, and integer `recordedAt`; otherwise throw `RangeError`. Sort by the requested field, ascending or descending. String fields use ordinary code-unit comparison. Equal keys retain source order. A page beyond the last page returns no items while preserving the requested page. Empty input has zero total pages. Returned items must be copies, and neither the source array nor its objects may be mutated.

Return only the complete source file; do not include Markdown fences or prose.

